      "content": "The volatility in West Africa is often rooted in the way these diverse societies are structured, which is fundamentally different from the more unified nations you mentioned. In many West African contexts, ethnic identity is deeply intertwined with political and economic access, making it a primary lens through which all major decisions are viewed. While other regions might manage internal disagreements through established, centralized institutions, the friction here often plays out along tribal lines, leading to more explosive and less predictable outcomes for outsiders.",
