    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So you're saying the tribalism itself is a factor that makes these markets inherently more prone to chaos compared to more cohesive societies. If we were doing a risk assessment, would you argue that these regions are just fundamentally more difficult to stabilize because of their ethnic makeup, or is it just a lack of institutions? Basically, is the ethnic complexity an inescapable risk factor for a long-term play there?",
